          "lineNumber": 492,
          "lineContent": "rec, err := scorer.Recommend(ctx, workspaceID, limit)",
          "title": "Invoke recommendation scorer",
          "description": "Skills layer calls overseer scorer to generate task recommendations"
        },
        {
          "id": "2b",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 90,
          "lineContent": "analyzer := tasksgraph.NewAnalyzer()",
          "title": "Create graph analyzer instance",
          "description": "Scorer instantiates tasksgraph analyzer for metrics computation"
        },
        {
          "id": "2c",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 103,
          "lineContent": "taskMailCounts := s.getTaskMailCounts(ctx, workspaceID, pending)",
          "title": "Retrieve mailbox message counts",
          "description": "Fetches unread admin/overseer message counts per task from blackboard store"
        },
        {
          "id": "2d",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 139,
          "lineContent": "normCritPath = float64(node.CriticalPathScore) / maxCritPath",
          "title": "Normalize critical path score",
          "description": "Normalizes critical path to 0-1 range for weighted scoring"
        },
        {
          "id": "2e",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 166,
          "lineContent": "score := WeightCriticalPath*normCritPath + WeightPageRank*normPageRank + WeightAdminMail*normAdmin + WeightOverseerMail*normOverseer + WeightRecency*recencyFactor",
          "title": "Compute weighted score",
          "description": "Applies scoring formula: 30% critical path, 20% PageRank, 25% admin mail, 15% overseer mail, 10% recency"
        },
        {
          "id": "2f",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 190,
          "lineContent": "sort.Slice(scores, func(i, j int) bool { return scores[i].Score \u003e scores[j].Score })",
          "title": "Sort by score descending",
          "description": "Orders tasks by final weighted score for prioritization"
        },
        {
          "id": "2g",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 208,
          "lineContent": "rec.TopRecommended = \u0026scores[0]",
          "title": "Set top recommendation",
          "description": "Returns highest-scored task as top recommendation"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Overseer Recommendation Scoring Flow\n├── Skills Layer (todo skill)\n│   └── scorer.Recommend() invocation \u003c-- 2a\n│\n└── Overseer Scorer (internal/analysis/overseer)\n    ├── Initialize analyzer \u003c-- 2b\n    │   └── tasksgraph.NewAnalyzer() \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:90\n    │\n    ├── Analyze graph\n    │   └── analyzer.Analyze(pending, ws) \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:91\n    │       └── [returns NodeMetrics with PageRank,\n    │            critical paths, degrees]\n    │\n    ├── Get mailbox counts \u003c-- 2c\n    │   └── s.getTaskMailCounts() \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:103\n    │       └── boardStore.CountMessagesByTask() \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:230\n    │           └── [returns admin, overseer, total]\n    │\n    ├── Normalize metrics\n    │   ├── Normalize critical path (0-1) \u003c-- 2d\n    │   ├── Normalize PageRank (0-1) \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:145\n    │   ├── Normalize mail counts (0-1) \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:159\n    │   └── Compute recency factor \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:154\n    │\n    ├── Apply scoring formula \u003c-- 2e\n    │   └── 30% critPath + 20% pageRank +\n    │       25% adminMail + 15% overseerMail +\n    │       10% recency\n    │\n    ├── Sort by score descending \u003c-- 2f\n    │\n    └── Set top recommendation \u003c-- 2g\n        └── return Recommendation \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:211",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nIn a multi-agent task management system, agents need to know **which task to work on next**. With dozens of pending tasks that have complex dependency relationships, simply picking the oldest or newest task is insufficient. The system needs to consider:\n\n- **Dependency blocking**: Tasks that block many others should be prioritized\n- **Graph centrality**: Tasks that are central to the dependency graph are more important\n- **Human attention**: When admins or the overseer send messages about a task, it needs urgent attention\n- **Staleness**: Recently updated tasks shouldn't be immediately re-prioritized\n\nThe **overseer scorer** [2a] solves this by computing a weighted score that combines graph analysis with mailbox state to produce ranked task recommendations.\n\n## Details\n\n### Scoring Formula\n\nThe scorer applies a **five-factor weighted formula** [2e]:\n- **30% Critical Path Score**: Longest dependency chain from this task to any leaf\n- **20% PageRank**: Graph centrality (tasks depended upon by many others rank higher)\n- **25% Admin Messages**: Unread messages from human administrators\n- **15% Overseer Messages**: Unread messages from the system overseer\n- **10% Recency Factor**: `1 / (1 + days_since_update)` to avoid stale tasks\n\n### Execution Flow\n\n1. **Graph Analysis** [2b]: The scorer instantiates a `tasksgraph.Analyzer` which builds a directed graph where edges represent dependencies (A→B means \"A depends on B\")\n\n2. **Metric Computation**: The analyzer computes PageRank using gonum's implementation with damping factor 0.85, and critical path scores via memoized DFS\n\n3. **Mailbox Integration** [2c]: The scorer queries the blackboard store to count unread messages per task, categorized by sender type (admin vs overseer)\n\n4. **Normalization** [2d]: All metrics are normalized to 0-1 range by dividing by the maximum value in the current task set, preventing score inflation\n\n5. **Scoring \u0026 Ranking** [2f]: Each task receives a weighted score, tasks are sorted descending, and the top recommendation is returned [2g]\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n**Normalization prevents unbounded scores**: Without normalizing mail counts, a task with 100 unread messages would dominate the score regardless of graph importance. By normalizing to the max in the current set, all factors contribute proportionally.\n\n**Separate admin/overseer weights**: Admin messages (25%) carry more weight than overseer messages (15%) because human attention signals are considered more critical than automated system notifications.\n\n**Critical path prioritization**: The 30% weight on critical path ensures that **blocking tasks** (those that prevent other work) naturally rise to the top of recommendations."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "title": "Mailbox Message Counting for Task Scoring",
      "description": "Blackboard storage system in internal/storage/blackboard - counts unread messages by sender type to boost task priority",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "3a",
          "path": "internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go",
          "lineNumber": 230,
          "lineContent": "admin, overseerCnt, total, err := s.boardStore.CountMessagesByTask(ctx, workspaceID, t.ID)",
          "title": "Query message counts per task",
          "description": "Scorer retrieves unread message counts grouped by sender type"
        },
        {
          "id": "3b",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 486,
          "lineContent": "rows, err := s.db.QueryContext(ctx, `SELECT sender FROM board_messages WHERE workspace_id = ? AND task_id = ? AND status IN (?, ?)`, workspaceID, taskID, agent.BoardMessageStatusUnread, agent.BoardMessageStatusSurfaced)",
          "title": "Execute message count query",
          "description": "Queries board_messages table for unread/surfaced messages by task"
        },
        {
          "id": "3c",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 503,
          "lineContent": "if agent.IsAdminSender(sender) { admin++ } else if agent.IsOverseerSender(sender) { overseer++ }",
          "title": "Classify sender types",
          "description": "Categorizes messages by sender: admin, overseer, or other"
        },
        {
          "id": "3d",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 509,
          "lineContent": "return admin, overseer, total, nil",
          "title": "Return categorized counts",
          "description": "Returns separate counts for admin, overseer, and total unread messages"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Mailbox Message Counting for Task Scoring\n└── Overseer Scorer (scorer.go)\n    └── getTaskMailCounts() iteration \u003c-- internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:229\n        └── CountMessagesByTask() call \u003c-- 3a\n            └── BoardStore (board_store.go)\n                ├── Query board_messages table \u003c-- 3b\n                │   └── Filter: workspace + task + unread\n                └── Process results loop \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:497\n                    ├── Classify sender type \u003c-- 3c\n                    │   ├── IsAdminSender() check \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:503\n                    │   └── IsOverseerSender() check \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:505\n                    └── Return counts \u003c-- 3d\n                        └── (admin, overseer, total)",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe overseer recommendation system needs to **prioritize tasks based on human attention signals**. When admins or the overseer system send messages about specific tasks, those tasks should be surfaced higher in recommendations. The mailbox message counting system [3a] solves this by **quantifying unread messages per task**, broken down by sender type (admin vs overseer), which then feeds into the weighted scoring formula that determines task priority.\n\n## Details\n\n### Message Query and Classification\n\nThe `CountMessagesByTask` method [3b] queries the `board_messages` table for a specific workspace and task, filtering for messages with status `unread` or `surfaced`. This captures messages that haven't been explicitly acknowledged by agents.\n\nThe query returns sender IDs, which are then **classified into three categories** [3c]:\n- **Admin messages** (weight: 25%) - identified by sender prefix `actor:admin:` or exact match `admin`\n- **Overseer messages** (weight: 15%) - identified by sender `actor:system:overseer`\n- **Other messages** - counted in total but not separately weighted\n\n### Integration with Scoring\n\nThe scorer iterates through all pending tasks [3a], calling `CountMessagesByTask` for each one. The returned counts [3d] are normalized (0-1 range) and multiplied by their respective weights before being combined with graph metrics (PageRank, critical path) and recency factors to produce the final task score.\n\nThis design ensures that **human intervention signals** (admin messages) have the strongest impact on task prioritization, followed by system-level coordination (overseer messages), allowing the recommendation system to respond to real-time communication patterns."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "title": "PageRank Persistence to Task Database",
      "description": "Task storage system in internal/storage/tasks - persists computed PageRank scores to SQLite for retrieval",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "4a",
          "path": "skills/todo/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 2024,
          "lineContent": "if err := store.SetPageRanks(ctx, ranks); err != nil {",
          "title": "Persist PageRank scores",
          "description": "Todo skill calls store to save computed PageRank values"
        },
        {
          "id": "4b",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 665,
          "lineContent": "tx, err := s.db.BeginTx(ctx, nil)",
          "title": "Begin transaction",
          "description": "Starts SQLite transaction for bulk PageRank updates"
        },
        {
          "id": "4c",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 673,
          "lineContent": "stmt, err := tx.PrepareContext(ctx, `UPDATE tasks SET pagerank = ? WHERE id = ?`)",
          "title": "Prepare update statement",
          "description": "Creates prepared statement for efficient bulk updates"
        },
        {
          "id": "4d",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 680,
          "lineContent": "if _, err := stmt.ExecContext(ctx, rank, id); err != nil {",
          "title": "Execute update for each task",
          "description": "Updates pagerank column for each task ID in the map"
        },
        {
          "id": "4e",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 685,
          "lineContent": "if err := tx.Commit(); err != nil {",
          "title": "Commit transaction",
          "description": "Atomically commits all PageRank updates to database"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "PageRank Persistence Flow\n├── Todo Skill (skills/todo/main.go)\n│   ├── updatePageRanksInBackground() \u003c-- skills/todo/main.go:2000\n│   │   ├── Compute graph insights \u003c-- skills/todo/main.go:2012\n│   │   ├── Build ranks map \u003c-- skills/todo/main.go:2018\n│   │   └── store.SetPageRanks() \u003c-- 4a\n│   └── Background goroutine trigger\n└── Task Store (internal/storage/tasks/store.go)\n    └── SetPageRanks(ctx, ranks) \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:660\n        ├── tx.BeginTx() \u003c-- 4b\n        ├── tx.PrepareContext(UPDATE) \u003c-- 4c\n        ├── Loop over ranks map \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:679\n        │   └── stmt.ExecContext(rank, id) \u003c-- 4d\n        └── tx.Commit() \u003c-- 4e",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nTask graphs in agentctl need **PageRank scores** to help prioritize work. When tasks have complex dependency relationships (A depends on B, C depends on A and D, etc.), the system needs to identify which tasks are most \"central\" or \"important\" based on how many other tasks depend on them. PageRank, borrowed from Google's web page ranking algorithm, provides exactly this metric—tasks that many other tasks depend on get higher scores.\n\nHowever, computing PageRank is expensive (it requires building a graph and running iterative algorithms), so the scores must be **persisted to the database** [4a] rather than recomputed on every query. This trace shows how computed PageRank values flow from the graph analysis layer into the SQLite task database.\n\n## Details\n\n### Background Computation\n\nThe `updatePageRanksInBackground()` function in the todo skill runs the PageRank computation asynchronously. It first calls the tasksgraph analyzer to compute metrics for all tasks in the workspace, then extracts just the PageRank scores into a map of `taskID -\u003e score` [4a].\n\n### Transactional Bulk Update\n\nThe `SetPageRanks()` method [4b] performs a **bulk update** using a SQLite transaction to ensure atomicity. It begins a transaction [4b], prepares a single UPDATE statement [4c], then executes it once per task [4d]. This prepared statement approach is more efficient than individual updates because the SQL is parsed only once.\n\nThe transaction ensures that either **all PageRank scores are updated or none are**—there's no partial state where some tasks have fresh scores and others have stale ones [4e].\n\n### Database Schema\n\nThe `tasks` table has a `pagerank` column (type REAL) that stores the computed score. This column is queried later by the overseer scorer to generate task recommendations, where PageRank contributes 20% of the final weighted score."
    },
    {
